A||||31||Cheever2||Idea for better movement of parts among us.||||3||
Z||000000||Cheever2||05-22-2001||11:52 AM||||(For those of us in North America anyway)<P>For a long time I have been perplexed at the difficulty in getting needed parts from a Fiero owner who has something, cross-country to another in need of it.  Currently we rely on expensive shipping, or the coincidence of someone going on a long trip in the same vicinity.  I have only thought of one alternative.<P>Bear with me here.  This will sound crazy at first but it's really simple, and I think it could work.  It would require one person or team to gather and maintain some information, call it a database if you want.<P>Let's survey all the Fiero owners we can reach, to ask "How far would you be willing to drive to be in one leg of a cross-country parts relay?"  The answers would be the names of cities in each direction.  I believe with the help of Forum members, FOLD members and Fiero clubs, we could show on a map enough overlap in everyone's driving radius to plot a course for much of the parts movements that are required.  It certainly could not be done quicker than the well-known shipping companies, but perhaps cheaper.  Maybe even big items like fastback clips, facias and wheels could be sent more efficiently.  And there would be less breakage because things will be handled by people who know Fieros and care what happens to the parts.<P>Once the information is in a central place, it would be up to the people sending & receiving a part to look up what it would take to get it relayed, and then contact those along the route to ask "can you make a pickup at <I>XXX</I> and take it to <I>ZZZ</I>?"<P>I don't know if I could handle administering such a plan, but maybe someone could.  Or two or three people who live near each other.  A simple list on a website should do it, the biggest job would be gathering the information.  But there's the idea.  What do ya think?  Besides the fact that I'm crazy, I mean.<P><BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||AusFiero||05-22-2001||12:08 PM||||Ok Cheever Im in.<BR>I'll do the LA to Sydney run. :P<BR>Anyone got a submarinised vehicle for sale?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||10
