Z||000015||Cheever2||05-22-2001||09:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR>I've got a problem regarding location where I could be the epicenter of parts delivery or routing.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I had thought of this, but didn't mention it since I didn't have an answer for it.  I can only say that if you get more requests than you can do, just say no or tell 'em it will have to wait.  And not everything would be going all the way across the U.S.  Some might be from California to Denver, for example, and some from St Louis to New York, thus you wouldn't be involved in either one of those. <P>A part wouldn't begin its journey unless all relay points have been contacted and agree.  That way someone's stuff won't be stuck in the middle of the desert or something.  Please remember I did say this won't be quick.  The dates will be up to the convenience of the people doing the carrying.<P>I appreciate the suggestion about the website, but I think that would be too complex.  And it wouldn't work for those who fear cyberspace.  It would put too much burden on the administrator, whose function should be to only gather and store the information of who is available to go where.  The responsibility of using that information belongs to the person who needs something transported, but at least now he knows who to contact.<P>Okay, I'm thinking this up while typing it, but here's the information that needs to be kept regarding the relay points:  <BR>- email or contact info <BR>- cities at the boundaries of where they're willing to go<BR>- if they require payment, how much they expect<BR>- limitations of size or weight they can carry<P>I gotta say this won't get off the ground if everybody along the route expects payment.  It would add up so quick as to be more than conventional shipping costs.  This is meant to be Fiero owners helping each other out.  If that's just a dream let me know right now.<BR>I won't be disappointed if my idea doesn't work, I won't take it personal.  I am still skeptical of its chances really.  So be honest with me.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||maryjane||05-22-2001||10:38 PM||||Sounds like you've got somethin started, Cheever. A lot of people make trips during the year anyway and could post where and when they are going. I'm leaving San Angelo myself next mo for Paris Tex to Hou then San Antonio and back to San Angelo. Make the trip several times a year. I'm in, but have to warn ya, I NEVER get rid of anything.<BR>Don & Jane||||reg||14
Z||000017||Cheever2||05-23-2001||10:56 AM||||Tell you what I'll do... <BR>I'll put up a simple webpage and take it from there.  We'll just find out if this will work or not.<P>Who wants to help?  I need a volunteer on the Fiero E-List to spread the word there.  I could use help contacting people in the FOLD database: the more who help, the less we would each have to do.  I need someone to send a form letter to all the clubs (e-mail of course).  And naturally, I need to hear from the rest of you PFF-ers who can be part of the relay - e-mail me.  chodges1@houston.rr.com<P>Also, somebody take charge of a contest to decide on a name for this little venture.<P>I got a lot of response on this, but it's going to take a lot more to make it happen.  Thanks for all your input so far.  This is a great bunch of people.<BR>||||reg||6
