Z||000025||RobertVol||05-23-2001||10:57 PM||||Actually, We already have a message board for our club. We post what we need and also if we are bidding on something on E bay, This helps so we dont out bid someone in our area that may have a need for something and also it helps us know what people are looking for so if we run acros it we can let our local Fiero Owners know about it. It works but it is ALOT of work. We password protected ours so only members can log in and add changes or other needs. Whoever takes ownwership of this will have their hands full......BIG TIME ! <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <BR>NEXT MEETING - May 26th, in Jacksonville<BR><A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||Cheever2||05-24-2001||12:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Whoever takes ownwership of this will have their hands full......BIG TIME !<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Well, I'm just going to take the information and list it on a web page.  Whomoever has a need for parts to be transported will use the information as needed.  The work for me will be to get the word out, then put the data in.  I suspect it may bring me a lot of email, but we'll see how it goes.  I just hope enough people can form links across North America to get the job done.  Many of our things will still be shipped the usual way, but this can help for those big items or for people who can't afford UPS, FedEx etc.  So I don't think the volunteers will be swamped with requests for constantly driving all over the place.  <P>I have started to write the website, and will let y'all know when it's up.  Until then, email me (or post here) if you can be one of the relay points.  And let me know which of the jobs you can help out with!<P>||||reg||1
